/-!
# Closed immersions between smooth schemes are étale-locally coordinate subspaces

Let `S` be a scheme and let `i : Y ⟶ X` be a closed immersion of schemes smooth over `S`.  Near
every point `y` of `Y` the immersion is, after an étale change of coordinates on `X`, the
inclusion of relative affine `m`-space into relative affine `(m + n)`-space as the vanishing
locus of the last `n` coordinates:  there is an open `U ⊆ X` containing `i y` and an étale
`π : U ⟶ 𝐀^{m+n}_S` over `S` for which the open subscheme `V = i⁻¹(U)` of `Y` is exactly the
scheme-theoretic inverse image `π⁻¹(𝐀^m_S)`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.coordinateSubspaceEmbedding` includes relative affine `m`-space into
  relative affine `(m + n)`-space as the locus where the last `n` coordinates vanish.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.coordinateSubspaceEmbedding_firstCoordinate` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.coordinateSubspaceEmbedding_lastCoordinate` identify the coordinate
  embedding on coordinates:  the first `m` pull back to the `m` coordinates of the subspace, the
  last `n` to zero.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.coordinateSubspaceEmbedding_isClosedImmersion`: the coordinate
  subspace is a closed subscheme.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_etale_coordinateSubspaceEmbedding_isPullback`: **Stacks tag
  0FUE.**

## The argument

Smoothness of `i ≫ f` gives, by Stacks tag 054L, an étale chart `q : V ⟶ 𝐀^m_S` of `Y` over `S`
on a neighbourhood of `y`, and shrinking the ambient scheme realises that neighbourhood as
`i⁻¹(U)` for an affine open `U ⊆ X`.  Since `i` is a closed immersion of schemes smooth over `S`
it is a regular immersion (Stacks tag 067U), hence Koszul-regular and so `H₁`-regular (Stacks tag
063K), so on a smaller affine open `W ⊆ U` the kernel of `i` on sections is generated by an
`H₁`-regular sequence `a₁, …, a_n` (Stacks tag 063G).  Lifting the `m` coordinates of
`q` through the surjection `Γ(W) ⟶ Γ(i⁻¹W)` and adjoining the `aₖ` as the last `n` coordinates
produces `π : W ⟶ 𝐀^{m+n}_S` over `S` making the square with `q` and the coordinate embedding
cartesian:  the `aₖ` generate the kernel, which is exactly the condition for the inverse image of
the coordinate subspace to be the closed subscheme.

What remains is étaleness of `π` near `y`, and it is here that regularity of the sequence is
used.  By Stacks tag 02GU it suffices to see that `π` is flat at the point and that its fibre
over the image residue field is étale.  The latter is automatic from the cartesian square,
because the fibre of `π` is isomorphic to the fibre of the étale `q`.  For the former, the
kernel of the coordinate embedding on stalks is generated by the last `n` coordinates
(`coordinateSubspaceEmbedding_ker_stalkMap`), whose images under `π` are the germs of the `aₖ`,
hence an `H₁`-regular sequence; the cartesian square identifies `𝒪_{V,y}` with
`𝒪_{W, i y} ⧸ (a)`, which is flat over `𝒪_{𝐀^m_S} ⧸ (coords)` because `q` is étale; and the
local criterion for flatness for a local homomorphism essentially of finite presentation
(Stacks tag 0471) upgrades that to flatness of `𝒪_{𝐀^{m+n}_S} ⟶ 𝒪_{W, i y}`.

## Implementation notes

The coordinates of relative affine space are indexed by `ULift.{u} (Fin d)` so that the index
type lies in the same universe as the schemes, which is what `AlgebraicGeometry.AffineSpace`
requires.  The coordinate subspace is the locus of `Fin.natAdd`-indexed coordinates, so that no
index arithmetic intervenes between the two blocks of variables.

The conclusion is phrased with `V = i⁻¹(U)` rather than with an abstract `V`:  `Y ∩ U` is the
scheme-theoretic inverse image, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.resLE` is the restriction of
`i` to it.  The equality `V = π⁻¹(𝐀^m_S)` and the commutativity of the right square are both
contained in the assertion that the square
```
V ⟶ 𝐀^m_S
↓        ↓
U ⟶ 𝐀^{m+n}_S
```
is cartesian; commutativity of the left square is the definition of `resLE`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FUE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FUE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 054L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/054L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 067U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/067U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02GU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02GU)
-/

